28	\begin{quote}
29	This chapter will include the Fortress static type inference mechanism.
30	\end{quote}
31	and the note that the chapter keeps:
32	\begin{quote}
33	\begin{itemize}
34	\item There seems to be a circular dependency between inference and
35	juxtaposition disambiguation -- you have to know if the subexpressions have
36	arrow types to disambiguate, but you can't do that without using inference,
37	which requires knowing how the variable of unknown type is used.
38	\item Type Inference (Dan's email titled ``Comments on a first reading of the
39	spec'' on 06/05/07)
40	\item Do we want to forbid such cases where type inference infers
41	\TYP{BottomType}s for static parameters?
42	\end{itemize}
43	\end{quote}
